{
  "uid": "tandem-relay",
  "title": "Tandem relay",
  "tags": [
    "tandem"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "2s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-10m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is the outbox keeping up?",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backlog \u2014 events waiting to publish",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.lag.count. A GLOBAL reading of the whole outbox, emitted by every relay instance, so this takes max() across instances \u2014 sum() would multiply the same backlog by the number of relays.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(tandem_outbox_lag_count)",
          "legendFormat": "waiting"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Oldest waiting event",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.lag.age_seconds. Rises whenever anything is stuck, including a single blocked aggregate chain that barely moves the backlog count \u2014 which is why the two lag gauges are read together.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(tandem_outbox_lag_age_seconds)",
          "legendFormat": "oldest"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Waiting: claimable vs blocked",
      "description": "The backlog split in two, as independent lines (NOT stacked: a stacked zero series is drawn on top of the other one, which makes a healthy backlog look entirely blocked). 'blocked' is tandem.outbox.blocked.count \u2014 rows behind a FAILED head, which no relay will ever claim; 'claimable' is the rest. Read this before trusting the two panels above: one terminal failure pins them both high for ever.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "blocked"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(tandem_outbox_lag_count) - max(tandem_outbox_blocked_count)",
          "legendFormat": "claimable"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "max(tandem_outbox_blocked_count)",
          "legendFormat": "blocked"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Throughput and errors",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Publish latency \u2014 insert to ack",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.publish.latency, one sample per successfully published row. p50/p95/p99 read off histogram_quantile over the summed bucket counts across every reporting instance \u2014 correct the way a client-computed percentile average across instances is not (LLD-micrometer \u00a72). Approximates the HLD \u00a710 KPI (COMMIT\u2192ack, p50 < 200ms / p99 < 1s at normal load), not an exact reading of it: created_at is stamped at INSERT, not COMMIT, and the two ends are read from different clocks (database vs. relay) \u2014 both push this reading up, never down.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(tandem_outbox_publish_latency_seconds_bucket[30s])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(tandem_outbox_publish_latency_seconds_bucket[30s])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(tandem_outbox_publish_latency_seconds_bucket[30s])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Publish rate",
      "description": "rate over tandem.outbox.published, a plain counter. Tandem computes no rate of its own \u2014 a throughput figure is a query, which is exactly why the meter carries no .rate suffix. Summed across instances: each counts only what it published.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(tandem_outbox_published_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "published/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Retries",
      "description": "rate over tandem.outbox.retry.count \u2014 retriable dispatch failures being rescheduled. A non-zero floor here with a healthy backlog usually means one bad downstream, not a sick relay.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 26
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "yellow"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(tandem_outbox_retry_count_total[30s]))",
          "legendFormat": "retries/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rows given up on",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.failed.count \u2014 a LIVE count of rows in FAILED, not a tally of failure events, so it drops back when a stuck row is replayed. Anything above zero needs a human.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "red"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(tandem_outbox_failed_count)",
          "legendFormat": "failed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Events published out of order",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.order_violation.count \u2014 the relay published an aggregate's events out of the order they were meant to go in: a row the application numbered is judged on that number, one written without a number on the order it was written in (HLD \u00a74.2). Operator replays are excluded, so anything above zero is a write-side bug, not a recovery action. This is the only place the violation is ever visible: the rows are left in perfect order in the table, so no query finds it afterwards \u2014 only the relay, as it publishes.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 42
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "red"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(tandem_outbox_order_violation_count_total)",
          "legendFormat": "out of order"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is the relay itself healthy?",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 50
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Worker threads alive, per instance",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.workers.active. The one genuinely PER-INSTANCE signal here \u2014 a series per relay, and a series that disappears is an instance that stopped reporting.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 51
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "tandem_outbox_workers_active",
          "legendFormat": "{{relay}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Worker cycle age \u2014 alive vs actually working",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.workers.cycle_age_seconds, per relay. Seconds since that instance's least-recently-progressed live worker last completed a claim cycle. workers.active alone cannot tell a working worker from one merely alive \u2014 a thread blocked in a call that never returns stays alive forever; this is the direct signal for that failure mode (HLD \u00a77).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 51
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 15
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "tandem_outbox_workers_cycle_age_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "{{relay}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Buckets with work and no live owner",
      "description": "tandem.outbox.bucket.uncovered \u2014 LEASE coordination only. Above zero means some buckets have pending rows that nobody currently owns: a coverage stall, the loud failure mode the virtual-bucket design was chosen for.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 59
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "yellow"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(tandem_outbox_bucket_uncovered)",
          "legendFormat": "uncovered"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Leases reclaimed",
      "description": "increase over tandem.outbox.lease_expired.count \u2014 rows recovered from an instance that died holding them. A steady trickle means instances are dying or stalling, not that recovery is broken.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 59
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(tandem_outbox_lease_expired_count_total[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "reclaimed/min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Published, total",
      "description": "sum(tandem.outbox.published) across instances.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 67
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "text"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(tandem_outbox_published_total)",
          "legendFormat": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Relay instances reporting",
      "description": "How many relays Prometheus is currently getting metrics from. Zero here, with a backlog on the panels above, is the case no relay-emitted gauge can tell you about on its own.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "tandem-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 67
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(up{job=\"tandem-relay\"} == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "instances"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "timepicker": {
    "refresh_intervals": [
      "1s",
      "2s",
      "5s",
      "10s",
      "30s",
      "1m",
      "5m",
      "15m",
      "30m",
      "1h",
      "2h",
      "1d"
    ]
  }
}
